Alden -

Confirming Eileen C is on the Wednesday Dec 9 schedule. Three day
turnaround as standard. Couple of items to handle on your end
before delivery.

DELIVERY
  Bring Eileen C to slip 7 on the inside dock by 16:00 Tuesday
  Dec 8. Yard closes at 17:00. If conditions push delivery into
  Wednesday morning, call ahead (207-555-0808) so we can hold
  the lift crew.

LIFT
  Wednesday Dec 9, 08:00 ET sharp. Lift gear and trailer
  scheduled around that. Late delivery means we slip the lift to
  the following morning and you absorb a half-day yard fee.

PRE-HAUL CHECKLIST (owner responsibility)
  (1) Fuel tank below half. Top off at your discretion post-haul.
  (2) Batteries pulled and stored in a heated space. Yard does
      not store batteries through winter.
  (3) All gear stripped from deck and cabin: traps, buoys, line,
      bait barrels, removable electronics. Items left aboard are
      not covered under yard liability.
  (4) Bottom cleaning and minor hull paint touch-up included in
      the standard fee.

DIAGNOSTIC
  Per your prior call, the Cummins 6BTA intermittent overheating
  goes on the work order. Our lead diesel mechanic will start
  the diagnostic at 09:00 Wednesday after the boat is on the
  hard. Expect a phone call with results around 11:00.

WORK ORDER
  Sign in person Wednesday morning between 07:30 and 08:00. Bring
    - Vessel documentation
    - Any parts you want installed
    - Your work-order draft if you prepared one
    - A pre-authorization threshold (dollar amount the mechanic
      can work up to without calling you for approval)

BILLING
  Standard haul-out fee billed against the Hanover account on
  file. Parts and additional diesel labor billed on the invoice,
  Net 30 from completion.

INSURANCE
  Your Hanover policy ordinarily covers in-yard storage during a
  short haul. If you have questions about coverage during the
  Wed-Fri window, contact Hanover directly. Yard does not act as
  intermediary.

Splash and sea-trial slots will be confirmed Thursday after the
diagnostic is closed out.

Thanks Alden.

